<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Emperor Wu of Liang</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">464–549</span> · <a href="/centuries/6th-century">6th century</a> · Also known as Liang Wudi</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emperor-wu-of-han">Emperor Wu</a> of Liang, born Xiao Yan, founded the Liang dynasty in southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a> and reigned from 502 to 549. A kinsman of the Southern Qi imperial house and one of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eight-friends-of-jingling">Eight Friends of Jingling</a>, he rebelled against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/xiao-baojuan">Xiao Baojuan</a> in 501 and took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jiankang">Jiankang</a>. A devout Buddhist patron, he presided over a long cultural flowering that ended when the rebel <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hou-jing">Hou Jing</a> besieged Jiankang, and he died a captive in 549.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/emperor-wu-of-liang.jpg" alt="Emperor Wu of Liang" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Liang_Wudi.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
